Package: backcast
Title: Extend Official Statistics Back Across Methodology Breaks
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Ferrya", email = "114243237+FerrumSL@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: When a statistics office changes how it measures something, it
    publishes the new-method series from some year on and the old one up to some
    year. This package extends the new series back with the published methods side
    by side (ratio splice, difference splice, interpolation after Prados de la
    Escosura, mixed splicing after de la Fuente, and an indicator regression),
    reports how far they disagree, measures each method's error where both series
    were published, and tests where a spliced series breaks.
